-- Applied live: 73 questions that mentioned NCLEX (template-generated 'NCLEX synthesis / first action / rule' items) rewritten as real clinical questions; answer keys unchanged.
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client taking warfarin has an INR (international normalized ratio) of 9.2 and blood in the urine. Which medication should the nurse anticipate the provider will order to reverse the effect of warfarin?$nx$, question=$nx$A client taking warfarin has an INR (international normalized ratio) of 9.2 and blood in the urine. Which medication should the nurse anticipate the provider will order to reverse the effect of warfarin?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Vitamin K (phytonadione)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Andexanet alfa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Protamine sulfate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Idarucizumab"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Vitamin K (phytonadione) is the reversal agent for warfarin. Protamine sulfate reverses heparin, andexanet alfa reverses factor Xa inhibitors such as rivaroxaban and apixaban, and idarucizumab reverses dabigatran. For life-threatening bleeding the provider may also order fresh frozen plasma or prothrombin complex concentrate.$nx$ WHERE id=2112;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client receiving a continuous heparin infusion becomes pale and anxious, with a heart rate of 124/min, a blood pressure of 84/50 mm Hg, and new abdominal distention. The nurse suspects internal bleeding. Which sequence of actions is correct?$nx$, question=$nx$A client receiving a continuous heparin infusion becomes pale and anxious, with a heart rate of 124/min, a blood pressure of 84/50 mm Hg, and new abdominal distention. The nurse suspects internal bleeding. Which sequence of actions is correct?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Stop the infusion, assess vital signs and bleeding, prepare protamine sulfate, then notify the provider"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Give protamine sulfate before assessing the client"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Notify the provider and keep the infusion running until orders are received"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Give a fluid bolus and recheck the aPTT (activated partial thromboplastin time) in 4 hours"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$With suspected bleeding on an anticoagulant, the nurse first stops the drug, then assesses vital signs and the source of bleeding, prepares the antidote (protamine sulfate for heparin), and then calls the provider. Following this order stops further harm quickly and prevents delays in treatment.$nx$ WHERE id=2120;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client on warfarin has a nosebleed that will not stop and an INR (international normalized ratio) of 8.5. Which antidote should the nurse prepare to administer?$nx$, question=$nx$A client on warfarin has a nosebleed that will not stop and an INR (international normalized ratio) of 8.5. Which antidote should the nurse prepare to administer?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Vitamin K (phytonadione)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Andexanet alfa"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Protamine sulfate"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Calcium gluconate"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Warfarin is reversed with vitamin K. Protamine sulfate is the antidote for heparin, andexanet alfa is used for factor Xa inhibitors, and calcium gluconate does not reverse any anticoagulant. Pairing each anticoagulant with its antidote is an important safety skill.$nx$ WHERE id=2136;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client on a continuous heparin infusion reports sudden flank pain. The heart rate is 120/min, the blood pressure is 86/52 mm Hg, and the skin is pale. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, question=$nx$A client on a continuous heparin infusion reports sudden flank pain. The heart rate is 120/min, the blood pressure is 86/52 mm Hg, and the skin is pale. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Document the findings and recheck in 1 hour"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Give protamine sulfate before assessing the client"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Call the provider and leave the infusion running until orders are received"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stop the heparin infusion"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$The first action with suspected internal bleeding is to stop the anticoagulant so no more drug is delivered. The nurse then assesses vital signs and bleeding, prepares the antidote, and calls the provider. The antidote is not given before assessment, and the infusion is never left running while waiting for orders.$nx$ WHERE id=2144;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client receiving a heparin infusion is suspected of internal bleeding. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client receiving a heparin infusion is suspected of internal bleeding. Which actions should the nurse take? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Give the antidote before assessing the client"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Prepare protamine sulfate and notify the provider"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop the infusion"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Assess for low blood pressure, rapid heart rate, pallor and bleeding"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Leave the infusion running until the provider calls back"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$The nurse stops the infusion, assesses for signs of bleeding (low blood pressure, fast heart rate, pallor, visible bleeding), prepares the antidote, and notifies the provider. The antidote is not given before assessment, and the infusion is never left running while waiting for a call back.$nx$ WHERE id=2170;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse is teaching new staff about anticoagulant safety. Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse is teaching new staff about anticoagulant safety. Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Reversal agents such as vitamin K and protamine sulfate should be readily available"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Anticoagulants do not require routine laboratory monitoring"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Each anticoagulant must be matched with its lab test, such as aPTT (activated partial thromboplastin time) for heparin and INR (international normalized ratio) for warfarin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Signs of bleeding can be reported at the end of the shift"}, {"id": "e", "text": "New signs of bleeding require immediate action"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Safe anticoagulant care requires correct pairing of each drug with its lab test, watching for bleeding, having the antidote ready, and escalating promptly. Anticoagulants need routine monitoring, and bleeding must never wait until the end of a shift.$nx$ WHERE id=2177;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client on a continuous anticoagulant infusion has dark, tarry stools and reports dizziness. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client on a continuous anticoagulant infusion has dark, tarry stools and reports dizziness. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Prepare the antidote and notify the provider"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Check blood pressure, heart rate and other signs of bleeding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop the infusion"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Call the provider before stopping the infusion"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Give the antidote before assessing the client"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Dark tarry stools suggest gastrointestinal bleeding. The nurse stops the anticoagulant, assesses the client, prepares the antidote, and notifies the provider. Calling first while the drug keeps infusing, or giving the antidote before assessing, are unsafe.$nx$ WHERE id=2194;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is planning care for a client who has just started an anticoagulant. Which items belong in the plan of care? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is planning care for a client who has just started an anticoagulant. Which items belong in the plan of care? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Report any bleeding at the end of the shift"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monitor the correct laboratory test for the prescribed drug"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Check for signs of bleeding and act immediately if they appear"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Know which antidote is available for the prescribed drug"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Skip routine laboratory monitoring after the first dose"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Anticoagulant safety depends on matching each drug with the right monitoring test, checking for bleeding, knowing the antidote, and escalating quickly. Bleeding is reported immediately, and routine monitoring continues for as long as the drug is taken.$nx$ WHERE id=2201;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with thromboangiitis obliterans (Buerger disease) has a toe with gangrene that is no longer viable. Which statement by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with thromboangiitis obliterans (Buerger disease) has a toe with gangrene that is no longer viable. Which statement by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"Smoking cessation counseling can wait until the tissue is lost.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Amputation may be needed, so tissue viability is monitored closely to time surgery.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"Amputation is never an option in this disease.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Heating pads on the toe will restore blood flow.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Amputation may be required when gangrene is not viable, so the nurse monitors tissue viability closely to decide when surgery is needed. Cessation counseling is never delayed, and heat can burn ischemic tissue because the client cannot sense it well.$nx$ WHERE id=2225;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A 30-year-old man who smokes a pack of cigarettes a day has painful, cold, pale feet and weak pedal pulses in both feet. The provider suspects Buerger disease. Which teaching should the nurse prioritize?$nx$, question=$nx$A 30-year-old man who smokes a pack of cigarettes a day has painful, cold, pale feet and weak pedal pulses in both feet. The provider suspects Buerger disease. Which teaching should the nurse prioritize?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Pulse and skin color changes are not related to how the disease progresses"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Checking for gangrene is a low priority"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stop all tobacco use and report signs of gangrene"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Quitting smoking can wait until tissue loss occurs"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$A young male smoker with ischemia in both limbs points to Buerger disease. The priority teaching is complete tobacco cessation and watching for gangrene. Frame all teaching around mandatory cessation and limb preservation.$nx$ WHERE id=2228;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with Buerger disease asks what is most important to keep from losing a limb. Which response by the nurse is correct?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with Buerger disease asks what is most important to keep from losing a limb. Which response by the nurse is correct?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"Stopping all tobacco use is the most important step.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Checking your pulses and skin color does not matter.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"Cutting back on smoking is enough.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"You can wait to quit until after tissue damage occurs.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Complete tobacco cessation is the key to limb preservation in Buerger disease. Cutting back is not enough, and waiting until tissue loss occurs allows the disease to progress.$nx$ WHERE id=2253;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse assesses a 29-year-old man who smokes and has ischemia in both legs. Which findings or actions are consistent with Buerger disease and its care? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse assesses a 29-year-old man who smokes and has ischemia in both legs. Which findings or actions are consistent with Buerger disease and its care? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "A young smoker with ischemia in both limbs is a key clue"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Monitoring for progression to gangrene is a priority"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stopping all tobacco use is the first intervention"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Smoking cessation is optional"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Gangrene monitoring is a low priority"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$A young male smoker with bilateral ischemia suggests Buerger disease. The first intervention is to stop all tobacco, and the nurse monitors for gangrene progression.$nx$ WHERE id=2278;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is caring for a client 1 day after coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) surgery and a client who has been discharged after percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) with a stent. Which plan is MOST appropriate?$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is caring for a client 1 day after coronary artery bypass graft (CABG) surgery and a client who has been discharged after percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) with a stent. Which plan is MOST appropriate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Reassess the CABG client less often because the first vital signs were stable"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Skip discharge teaching because education has little effect on outcomes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Monitor the CABG client for tamponade, reinforce sternal precautions, and teach the PCI client to take dual antiplatelet therapy as prescribed"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Stop checking for tamponade after the first 24 hours"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$After CABG (coronary artery bypass graft) the highest-risk preventable complications are cardiac tamponade and sternal wound problems, so the nurse monitors for tamponade and enforces sternal precautions. After a stent, taking dual antiplatelet therapy exactly as prescribed prevents stent thrombosis.$nx$ WHERE id=2328;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse reviews priorities for a client 12 hours after CABG (coronary artery bypass graft) and a client 2 days after receiving a stent. Which statement reflects the priorities for these clients?$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse reviews priorities for a client 12 hours after CABG (coronary artery bypass graft) and a client 2 days after receiving a stent. Which statement reflects the priorities for these clients?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Taking medication is optional after a stent"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tamponade monitoring is not needed after CABG"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Education after a procedure has little effect on outcomes"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The CABG client needs tamponade monitoring, and the stent client needs to keep taking dual antiplatelet therapy"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Tamponade assessment is a priority after CABG (coronary artery bypass graft), and strict adherence to dual antiplatelet therapy is a priority after PCI (percutaneous coronary intervention) with a stent. Stopping those drugs early can cause the stent to clot.$nx$ WHERE id=2353;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which actions are priorities for clients after cardiac procedures? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$Which actions are priorities for clients after cardiac procedures? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Sternal precautions after CABG (coronary artery bypass graft)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Taking dual antiplatelet therapy as prescribed after PCI (percutaneous coronary intervention)"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tamponade monitoring is not needed after CABG (coronary artery bypass graft)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Assessing for cardiac tamponade after CABG (coronary artery bypass graft)"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Stopping antiplatelet drugs once chest pain is gone"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$After CABG (coronary artery bypass graft) the nurse enforces sternal precautions and assesses for tamponade. After PCI (percutaneous coronary intervention) the client must keep taking dual antiplatelet therapy even when symptoms resolve, because stopping early risks stent thrombosis.$nx$ WHERE id=2378;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is reviewing cardiac biomarkers with a nursing student. Which statement is MOST accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is reviewing cardiac biomarkers with a nursing student. Which statement is MOST accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Troponin is the gold standard for myocardial infarction, and CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) is best for detecting reinfarction"}, {"id": "b", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) replaces troponin to confirm myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Serial rechecks are unnecessary when the first value is borderline"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Myoglobin is the most specific marker for myocardial infarction"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Troponin is the gold standard and stays elevated the longest. CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) is best for reinfarction because it returns to normal sooner, BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) helps tell heart failure from other causes of dyspnea, and myoglobin rises earliest but is not specific. Match the marker to the clinical question.$nx$ WHERE id=2426;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client's BUN (blood urea nitrogen) is 38 mg/dL and the creatinine is 1.0 mg/dL. Which interpretation by the nurse is MOST accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client's BUN (blood urea nitrogen) is 38 mg/dL and the creatinine is 1.0 mg/dL. Which interpretation by the nurse is MOST accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Dehydration is likely, and following both values over time helps separate it from kidney damage"}, {"id": "b", "text": "These values confirm intrinsic kidney failure"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A high BUN with a normal creatinine proves a myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Serial rechecks are unnecessary when a value is borderline"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Normal BUN (blood urea nitrogen) is about 7–20 mg/dL and normal creatinine is 0.6–1.2 mg/dL. A high BUN with a normal creatinine suggests dehydration, while both high suggest kidney impairment. Trends help separate a prerenal cause from intrinsic kidney decline.$nx$ WHERE id=2445;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client has shortness of breath and the cause is unclear. Which laboratory test helps the nurse tell whether heart failure is the cause?$nx$, question=$nx$A client has shortness of breath and the cause is unclear. Which laboratory test helps the nurse tell whether heart failure is the cause?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Myoglobin"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Total CK (creatine kinase)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hemoglobin A1C (glycated hemoglobin)"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) rises when the ventricles are stretched and helps tell heart failure from other causes of dyspnea. Troponin and CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) are used for myocardial injury, and myoglobin rises early but is not specific.$nx$ WHERE id=2449;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is teaching a student about troponin. Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is teaching a student about troponin. Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) is the gold standard for myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Troponin stays elevated longer than other cardiac markers"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Troponin is the gold standard for myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Troponin is both highly sensitive and specific"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Myoglobin is more specific than troponin"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Troponin is the most sensitive and specific biomarker for myocardial infarction, it stays elevated the longest, and it is the gold standard. BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) is used for heart failure, and myoglobin rises early but is not specific.$nx$ WHERE id=2456;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which statements about cardiac biomarkers are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$Which statements about cardiac biomarkers are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Myoglobin is the best marker for reinfarction"}, {"id": "b", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) replaces troponin to confirm myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) is favored for detecting reinfarction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Troponin is the top marker for myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "e", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) and myoglobin serve different purposes"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Troponin is the gold standard for myocardial infarction, CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) is best for reinfarction, BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) helps differentiate heart failure as a cause of dyspnea, and myoglobin is the earliest but nonspecific marker. Each marker answers a different clinical question.$nx$ WHERE id=2476;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with chest pain asks about troponin. Which statements by the nurse are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client with chest pain asks about troponin. Which statements by the nurse are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"Myoglobin is more specific than troponin.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Troponin is both highly sensitive and specific.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) is the gold standard for a heart attack.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Troponin is the gold standard for a heart attack.\""}, {"id": "e", "text": "\"Troponin is drawn serially so we can follow the trend.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Troponin is the most specific and sensitive biomarker for myocardial infarction and is the gold standard. Serial levels show the trend. BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) is used for heart failure, and myoglobin is less specific.$nx$ WHERE id=2479;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client is admitted with suspected acute coronary syndrome. Which statements about cardiac biomarkers are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client is admitted with suspected acute coronary syndrome. Which statements about cardiac biomarkers are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) and myoglobin have different roles"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Myoglobin is the best marker for reinfarction"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Troponin is the top marker for myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "d", "text": "CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) is favored for detecting reinfarction"}, {"id": "e", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) replaces troponin to confirm myocardial infarction"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Troponin is the gold standard and longest lasting, CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB) is best for reinfarction, BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) helps differentiate heart failure as the cause of dyspnea, and myoglobin is earliest but nonspecific.$nx$ WHERE id=2499;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is reviewing a client's laboratory results. Which statements about troponin are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is reviewing a client's laboratory results. Which statements about troponin are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Troponin stays elevated longer than CK-MB (creatine kinase-MB)"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Troponin is both highly sensitive and specific"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Myoglobin is more specific than troponin"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Troponin is the gold standard for myocardial infarction"}, {"id": "e", "text": "BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) is the gold standard for myocardial infarction"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Troponin is the most sensitive and specific marker for myocardial infarction, stays elevated for days, and is the gold standard. BNP (B-type natriuretic peptide) is used for heart failure, and myoglobin is less specific.$nx$ WHERE id=2502;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client 2 days after cardiac surgery has muffled heart sounds, distended neck veins, and a blood pressure that has fallen from 118/76 to 82/60 mm Hg. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, question=$nx$A client 2 days after cardiac surgery has muffled heart sounds, distended neck veins, and a blood pressure that has fallen from 118/76 to 82/60 mm Hg. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Begin routine discharge teaching"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Document the findings and recheck in 1 hour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Wait because the risk of rapid decline is low"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Notify the provider immediately and prepare for pericardiocentesis"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$These findings suggest cardiac tamponade. The first action is to notify the provider immediately and prepare for pericardiocentesis, because delay can lead to cardiac arrest within minutes. Do not delay life-saving decompression for low-priority tasks.$nx$ WHERE id=2528;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with cardiac tamponade has fluid removed by pericardiocentesis. Which action is MOST appropriate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with cardiac tamponade has fluid removed by pericardiocentesis. Which action is MOST appropriate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Send the pericardial fluid for culture, cytology and chemistry"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Discard the fluid because analysis is unnecessary after aspiration"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Send only a glucose level"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hold the fluid at the bedside until the next shift"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Pericardial fluid is sent for culture, cytology and chemistry to find the cause. Emergency stabilization is paired with an etiology workup.$nx$ WHERE id=2551;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with suspected cardiac tamponade has a falling blood pressure and distended neck veins. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client with suspected cardiac tamponade has a falling blood pressure and distended neck veins. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Observe the client without intervening"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Recognize that delay can lead to cardiac arrest within minutes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Begin routine discharge teaching"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Prepare for pericardiocentesis"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Notify the provider immediately"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Cardiac tamponade is life threatening, so the nurse notifies the provider immediately and prepares for pericardiocentesis. Observation alone or routine tasks can allow rapid deterioration.$nx$ WHERE id=2578;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse listens to a client's heart and identifies S1 (first heart sound). Which statement is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse listens to a client's heart and identifies S1 (first heart sound). Which statement is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "S1 marks the end of systole"}, {"id": "b", "text": "S1 (\"lub\") is the closing of the mitral and tricuspid valves at the start of systole"}, {"id": "c", "text": "S1 is the closing of the aortic and pulmonic valves"}, {"id": "d", "text": "S1 is blood rushing into the ventricles during early filling"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$S1 ("lub") is produced by closure of the mitral and tricuspid valves at the start of systole. S2 ("dub") is closure of the aortic and pulmonic valves at the end of systole. Timing heart sounds with valve events helps interpret the cardiac cycle.$nx$ WHERE id=2721;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse teaches students a memory aid for abnormal heart sounds. Which statement is correct?$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse teaches students a memory aid for abnormal heart sounds. Which statement is correct?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) sounds like \"Ken-tuc-ky\" and is linked to heart failure, and S4 (fourth heart sound) sounds like \"Ten-nes-see\" and is linked to a stiff ventricle or hypertension"}, {"id": "b", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) sounds like \"Ten-nes-see\" and S4 (fourth heart sound) sounds like \"Ken-tuc-ky\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) and S4 (fourth heart sound) are both normal findings in all older adults"}, {"id": "d", "text": "S4 (fourth heart sound) sounds like \"Ken-tuc-ky\" and indicates fluid overload"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$S3 ("Ken-tuc-ky") is associated with heart failure and volume overload, and S4 ("Ten-nes-see") is associated with a stiff, noncompliant ventricle such as in hypertension. The memory aid helps students recall which gallop fits which problem.$nx$ WHERE id=2726;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nursing student asks what produces the first heart sound. Which explanation by the nurse is correct?$nx$, question=$nx$A nursing student asks what produces the first heart sound. Which explanation by the nurse is correct?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "The mitral and tricuspid valves close at the start of ventricular contraction"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The aortic and pulmonic valves close as the ventricles relax"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The ventricles fill rapidly during early diastole"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The atria stretch against a stiff ventricle"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$S1 ("lub") is the closing of the mitral and tricuspid valves at the start of systole. The closing of the aortic and pulmonic valves makes S2 (second heart sound).$nx$ WHERE id=2745;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with heart failure has an extra heart sound with the rhythm "Ken-tuc-ky." Which heart sound is this, and what does it suggest?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with heart failure has an extra heart sound with the rhythm "Ken-tuc-ky." Which heart sound is this, and what does it suggest?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "S3 (third heart sound), a sign of heart failure"}, {"id": "b", "text": "S4 (fourth heart sound), a sign of a stiff ventricle"}, {"id": "c", "text": "S1 (first heart sound), normal closing of the mitral valve"}, {"id": "d", "text": "S2 (second heart sound), a sign of aortic stenosis"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$"Ken-tuc-ky" is the S3 (third heart sound) gallop, which is linked to heart failure. S4 ("Ten-nes-see") is linked to a stiff ventricle or hypertension.$nx$ WHERE id=2750;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is teaching a student about gallop sounds. Which points should be included? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is teaching a student about gallop sounds. Which points should be included? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "S4 (fourth heart sound) fits the rhythm \"Ten-nes-see\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "S4 (fourth heart sound) is a normal finding in young adults"}, {"id": "c", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) points to heart failure, and S4 (fourth heart sound) points to a stiff ventricle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) fits the rhythm \"Ten-nes-see\""}, {"id": "e", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) fits the rhythm \"Ken-tuc-ky\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$S3 ("Ken-tuc-ky") is linked to heart failure, and S4 ("Ten-nes-see") is linked to stiff ventricles and hypertension. The two sounds point to different problems.$nx$ WHERE id=2776;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse is listening to the heart of a client with long-standing hypertension. Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse is listening to the heart of a client with long-standing hypertension. Which statements are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "S4 (fourth heart sound) is linked to normal youthful physiology"}, {"id": "b", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) fits the rhythm \"Ten-nes-see\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "S4 (fourth heart sound) fits the rhythm \"Ten-nes-see\" and suggests a stiff ventricle"}, {"id": "d", "text": "S3 (third heart sound) fits the rhythm \"Ken-tuc-ky\""}, {"id": "e", "text": "The two sounds point to different problems: S3 (third heart sound) to heart failure and S4 (fourth heart sound) to a stiff ventricle"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$S3 ("Ken-tuc-ky") suggests heart failure, and S4 ("Ten-nes-see") suggests a stiff ventricle, which is common in hypertension.$nx$ WHERE id=2800;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client in the intensive care unit has a blood pressure of 78/44 mm Hg and a mean arterial pressure (MAP) of 55 mm Hg. Which nursing action is the priority?$nx$, question=$nx$A client in the intensive care unit has a blood pressure of 78/44 mm Hg and a mean arterial pressure (MAP) of 55 mm Hg. Which nursing action is the priority?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Wait to see whether the MAP rises on its own"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Take no action unless the MAP falls below 20"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Treat the low MAP as urgent: notify the provider and support blood pressure and oxygenation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Assume perfusion is adequate and reassess in 4 hours"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$A MAP (mean arterial pressure) below 60 mmHg means organs are at risk of ischemia, so immediate blood pressure and oxygenation support is the priority. A MAP below 60 is an urgent perfusion threat.$nx$ WHERE id=2828;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with hypotension from blood loss has a blood pressure of 82/50 mm Hg. Which intervention is MOST appropriate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with hypotension from blood loss has a blood pressure of 82/50 mm Hg. Which intervention is MOST appropriate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Place the client upright in a chair"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reassess in 4 hours because perfusion appears stable"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Restore circulating volume with IV (intravenous) fluids or blood products while treating the cause"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Encourage quick position changes to raise the blood pressure"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Management of hypotension includes treating the cause, giving IV (intravenous) fluids or blood products for hypovolemia, using vasopressors for severe cases, positioning supine with the legs elevated, and changing position slowly.$nx$ WHERE id=2849;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client's mean arterial pressure (MAP) is 52 mmHg. Which statement by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client's mean arterial pressure (MAP) is 52 mmHg. Which statement by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"A MAP below 60 is an urgent threat to organ perfusion.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Large swings in blood pressure are always preferred.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"The MAP is the same as the systolic pressure.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"No action is needed unless the MAP is below 20.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$A MAP (mean arterial pressure) below 60 mmHg means organs are at risk of ischemia, so it is treated as an urgent perfusion threat with immediate blood pressure and oxygenation support.$nx$ WHERE id=2853;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client has a mean arterial pressure (MAP) of 54 mmHg. Which actions or statements are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client has a mean arterial pressure (MAP) of 54 mmHg. Which actions or statements are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "No action is needed unless the MAP is below 20"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Oxygenation support is also a priority"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Immediate blood pressure support is a priority"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A MAP below 60 puts organs at risk of ischemia"}, {"id": "e", "text": "A MAP of 55 gives acceptable organ perfusion"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$A MAP (mean arterial pressure) below 60 mmHg puts organs at risk of ischemia, and immediate blood pressure and oxygenation support is the priority.$nx$ WHERE id=2878;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with chest pain and suspected acute coronary syndrome asks why aspirin is given right away. Which response by the nurse is correct?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with chest pain and suspected acute coronary syndrome asks why aspirin is given right away. Which response by the nurse is correct?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"Aspirin can wait until the serial test results are back.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Aspirin is an antiplatelet drug that is given immediately because it lowers the risk of death from a heart attack.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"Aspirin is swallowed whole and given after the pain stops.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Aspirin is given only to relieve the pain.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Aspirin 325 mg is given immediately and chewed so it is absorbed quickly. Immediate antiplatelet therapy is a front-line step that reduces mortality.$nx$ WHERE id=2925;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client reports crushing chest pain that spreads to the left arm. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, question=$nx$A client reports crushing chest pain that spreads to the left arm. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Review the client's risk factors for coronary artery disease"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Obtain a 12-lead electrocardiogram and notify the provider, and give chewed aspirin as ordered"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Check the potency of the nitroglycerin before any other action"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wait for serial enzymes before getting an electrocardiogram"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$For chest pain the first actions are a 12-lead electrocardiogram and notifying the provider, and aspirin is given immediately and chewed. Rhythm and injury assessment and antiplatelet therapy should not be delayed.$nx$ WHERE id=2929;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse is giving aspirin to a client with suspected acute coronary syndrome. Which statement is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse is giving aspirin to a client with suspected acute coronary syndrome. Which statement is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Aspirin should be delayed until the troponin result is back"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Aspirin 325 mg is chewed right away because immediate antiplatelet therapy lowers mortality"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Aspirin is contraindicated in all acute coronary syndrome cases"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Aspirin should be swallowed whole"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Aspirin 325 mg is given immediately and chewed. Immediate antiplatelet therapy is a front-line mortality-reduction step.$nx$ WHERE id=2951;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with infective endocarditis asks how long treatment will last. Which response by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with infective endocarditis asks how long treatment will last. Which response by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"You will take oral antibiotics for about 5 days.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"You will need IV (intravenous) antibiotics for 4 to 6 weeks, chosen for the organism, with repeat cultures to confirm the infection is cleared.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"A 3-day oral course is enough.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Blood cultures are drawn after several antibiotic doses.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Treatment requires IV (intravenous) antibiotics for 4 to 6 weeks with organism-specific regimens and culture-confirmed clearance. Cultures are drawn before antibiotics begin, and prolonged IV adherence and follow-up cultures are essential.$nx$ WHERE id=3022;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client has a fever, a new regurgitant murmur, positive blood cultures and splinter hemorrhages. Which action should the nurse anticipate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client has a fever, a new regurgitant murmur, positive blood cultures and splinter hemorrhages. Which action should the nurse anticipate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Observation because the risk of emboli is minimal"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Urgent workup and treatment for infective endocarditis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Delay treatment until the cultures are repeated"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Rule out endocarditis because emboli are present"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Fever, a new regurgitant murmur, positive cultures and embolic signs form a high-risk cluster that should trigger an urgent workup and treatment for infective endocarditis. Clustered red flags are treated as a high-acuity syndrome.$nx$ WHERE id=3027;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse is reviewing findings for a client with possible infective endocarditis. Which cluster of findings should prompt an urgent workup?$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse is reviewing findings for a client with possible infective endocarditis. Which cluster of findings should prompt an urgent workup?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Mild fatigue and a normal temperature"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Morning joint stiffness that improves with movement"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fever, a new murmur and positive blood cultures"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A soft, unchanged murmur present since childhood"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Fever with a new murmur and positive blood cultures is the classic pattern of infective endocarditis and should trigger an urgent workup. Embolic signs raise suspicion further.$nx$ WHERE id=3051;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client has a fever and a new heart murmur. Which findings support infective endocarditis? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client has a fever and a new heart murmur. Which findings support infective endocarditis? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Emboli make the diagnosis less likely"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Positive cultures mean treatment should be delayed"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Embolic signs, such as splinter hemorrhages, raise concern for active infection"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Fever with a new murmur is a key cluster"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Positive blood cultures add urgency"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Fever with a new regurgitant murmur, positive cultures and embolic signs together should trigger an urgent workup and treatment for infective endocarditis. Emboli and positive cultures raise concern and urgency rather than lowering it.$nx$ WHERE id=3077;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse plans care for a client with suspected infective endocarditis. Which items should be included? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse plans care for a client with suspected infective endocarditis. Which items should be included? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Embolic signs lower the suspicion of endocarditis"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Positive blood cultures add urgency to treatment"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Fever with a new murmur is a key cluster of findings"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Embolic signs, such as splinter hemorrhages, increase concern for active infection"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Positive cultures should delay treatment"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Fever, a new murmur, positive cultures and embolic signs should trigger an urgent workup and treatment. Positive cultures and embolic signs increase urgency.$nx$ WHERE id=3101;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse finds an adult client unresponsive with no pulse. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse finds an adult client unresponsive with no pulse. Which action should the nurse take FIRST?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Wait because the client's symptoms were mild earlier"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Observe the client for 5 minutes"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Call for help and begin chest compressions without delay"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Check the rhythm for several minutes before starting compressions"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$If there is no pulse the nurse starts CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) immediately and does not delay compressions to check the rhythm. Immediate compressions outrank diagnostic steps in a pulseless client.$nx$ WHERE id=3126;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$During a cardiac arrest the nurse reviews possible causes. Which statement is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$During a cardiac arrest the nurse reviews possible causes. Which statement is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Reversible causes should be sought while high-quality CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) continues"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Rhythm assessment should always come before compressions in a pulseless client"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A drug overdose cannot cause cardiac arrest"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Cardiac arrest is caused only by myocardial infarction"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Cardiac arrest can be triggered by myocardial infarction, electrolyte imbalance, drowning and drug overdose. The team looks for reversible causes while running high-quality CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation).$nx$ WHERE id=3145;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$An adult is pulseless. Which statement explains why compressions begin before a rhythm check?$nx$, question=$nx$An adult is pulseless. Which statement explains why compressions begin before a rhythm check?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Rhythm assessment should always precede compressions"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The rhythm must be checked for several minutes before compressions can help"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Compressions are started only after the family is notified"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Compressions keep blood flowing to the brain and heart, so they take priority over diagnostic steps"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Immediate compressions maintain blood flow to the brain and heart, so they outrank delayed diagnostic steps in a pulseless client.$nx$ WHERE id=3151;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse finds a client with no pulse. Which actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse finds a client with no pulse. Which actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Do not let a rhythm check delay the first compressions"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Call for help and activate the code team"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Observe the client without intervening"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Start CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) immediately"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Check the rhythm for several minutes before compressions"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$No pulse means CPR (cardiopulmonary resuscitation) starts right away and a rhythm check must not delay the first compressions. The nurse also calls for help.$nx$ WHERE id=3176;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with a pacemaker becomes hypotensive and dizzy, with a blood pressure of 78/46 mm Hg. Which position should the nurse use?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with a pacemaker becomes hypotensive and dizzy, with a blood pressure of 78/46 mm Hg. Which position should the nurse use?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Trendelenburg position"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Standing at the bedside"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Sitting upright with the legs dangling"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Supine with the legs elevated 15 to 30 degrees"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$For hypotension or shock, position the client supine with the legs elevated 15 to 30 degrees to increase venous return. Trendelenburg is not recommended, and sitting or standing lowers blood pressure further.$nx$ WHERE id=3224;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with an implanted cardiac device becomes hypotensive and short of breath. Which approach is the nursing priority?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with an implanted cardiac device becomes hypotensive and short of breath. Which approach is the nursing priority?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Reassess later because the symptoms come and go"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Complete the documentation before supporting circulation"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Stabilize airway, breathing and circulation before noncritical steps"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Wait for the device clinic to open to check the pacemaker"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Airway, breathing and circulation come first. Oxygenation and circulation are supported before any noncritical step, and Trendelenburg is avoided for hypotension.$nx$ WHERE id=3229;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client is hypotensive. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client is hypotensive. Which nursing actions are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Support oxygenation first"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Avoid placing the client in Trendelenburg position"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Support circulation"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Place the client in Trendelenburg for all hypotension"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Complete documentation before supporting circulation"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Oxygenation and circulation are prioritized first, and Trendelenburg is avoided for hypotension. Documentation never comes before circulation.$nx$ WHERE id=3279;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A 32-year-old reports sharp chest pain that eases when leaning forward. The provider suspects pericarditis. Which assessments should the nurse prioritize?$nx$, question=$nx$A 32-year-old reports sharp chest pain that eases when leaning forward. The provider suspects pericarditis. Which assessments should the nurse prioritize?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Treat the complaint as a gastrointestinal problem"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tamponade monitoring is unnecessary in pericarditis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The pain pattern, a friction rub, the electrocardiogram, and signs of tamponade"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The electrocardiogram can be skipped in chest pain with suspected pericarditis"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$In suspected pericarditis the nurse recognizes the pain pattern, listens for a friction rub, interprets the electrocardiogram, and watches for tamponade. This separates it from myocardial infarction and detects complications early.$nx$ WHERE id=3326;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with suspected pericarditis has chest pain that is relieved by sitting forward. Which approach is MOST appropriate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with suspected pericarditis has chest pain that is relieved by sitting forward. Which approach is MOST appropriate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Skip the electrocardiogram because the pain is positional"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Tamponade monitoring is unnecessary in pericarditis"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Assess the pain pattern, listen for a friction rub, review the electrocardiogram, and watch for tamponade"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Manage tamponade with observation only"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Care in suspected pericarditis centers on the pain pattern, a friction rub, the electrocardiogram, and tamponade surveillance. Tamponade is an emergency and is not managed by observation alone.$nx$ WHERE id=3350;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which items belong in the plan of care for a client with suspected pericarditis? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$Which items belong in the plan of care for a client with suspected pericarditis? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Monitor for progression to effusion or tamponade"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Note the pain pattern and how it changes with position"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Tamponade monitoring is unnecessary in pericarditis"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Listen for a friction rub and review the electrocardiogram"}, {"id": "e", "text": "The electrocardiogram can be ignored in chest pain"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Pain pattern and position response, a friction rub, and electrocardiogram changes are high-value assessments, and the nurse monitors for progression to effusion or tamponade.$nx$ WHERE id=3376;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$For a client with suspected pericarditis, which statements are correct? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$For a client with suspected pericarditis, which statements are correct? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Monitor for progression to effusion or tamponade"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A friction rub and electrocardiogram changes are high-value assessments"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Pain that changes with position is a key clue"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The electrocardiogram can be ignored in chest pain with suspected pericarditis"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Tamponade monitoring is unnecessary in pericarditis"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$In suspected pericarditis the nurse prioritizes pain pattern recognition, friction rub assessment, electrocardiogram interpretation, and tamponade surveillance.$nx$ WHERE id=3400;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client is diagnosed with a deep vein thrombosis (DVT). Which statement about anticoagulation is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client is diagnosed with a deep vein thrombosis (DVT). Which statement about anticoagulation is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"Anticoagulation lasts only 1 day.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"An antiplatelet drug alone treats a DVT.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"Heparin is started first, then warfarin or a direct oral anticoagulant continues for 3 to 6 months.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Therapy stops when the swelling goes down.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$DVT (deep vein thrombosis) treatment starts with heparin and then continues with warfarin or a non-vitamin K oral anticoagulant for 3 to 6 months. The nurse helps the client move safely from acute to maintenance anticoagulation.$nx$ WHERE id=3421;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client 1 day after a femoral bypass has a cool, pale foot with no pedal pulse. Which nursing action is the priority?$nx$, question=$nx$A client 1 day after a femoral bypass has a cool, pale foot with no pedal pulse. Which nursing action is the priority?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Massage the leg to improve blood flow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Elevate the leg above the heart and recheck in 1 hour"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Report the six Ps (pain, pallor, pulselessness, paresthesia, paralysis, poikilothermia) to the provider immediately"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Recheck the pulses at the next shift"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$The six Ps indicate an arterial emergency, so the nurse notifies the provider immediately to find limb-threatening ischemia and prevent embolization. The leg is not massaged, and pulses are reassessed after vascular interventions.$nx$ WHERE id=3427;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with a newly diagnosed DVT (deep vein thrombosis) asks about treatment. Which response by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with a newly diagnosed DVT (deep vein thrombosis) asks about treatment. Which response by the nurse is accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"You will receive heparin first, then take warfarin or another oral anticoagulant for 3 to 6 months.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"A daily aspirin alone treats a DVT.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"Treatment stops after 24 hours.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Treatment is complete once the leg swelling is gone.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$DVT (deep vein thrombosis) treatment begins with heparin and then continues with warfarin or a direct oral anticoagulant for 3 to 6 months.$nx$ WHERE id=3445;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which nursing priority applies to a client with an acute arterial blockage in a limb?$nx$, question=$nx$Which nursing priority applies to a client with an acute arterial blockage in a limb?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Prevent embolization and quickly identify limb-threatening ischemia"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Check pulses only at the next shift"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Observe pain, pallor and coolness without notifying the provider"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Escalate only when both limbs are affected"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$The six Ps are treated as an arterial emergency. The nurse assesses pulses before and after interventions, avoids massaging a possible clot, and reports findings immediately.$nx$ WHERE id=3451;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which nursing actions are appropriate for clients with vascular conditions? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$Which nursing actions are appropriate for clients with vascular conditions? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Massage a leg with a suspected DVT (deep vein thrombosis) to improve flow"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Report the six Ps of an acute arterial blockage right away"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Never massage a leg with a suspected DVT (deep vein thrombosis)"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Observe the six Ps without notifying the provider"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Check pulses before and after a vascular procedure"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$A suspected DVT (deep vein thrombosis) leg is never massaged because the clot could travel. The six Ps are an arterial emergency and are reported immediately, and pulses are assessed before and after interventions.$nx$ WHERE id=3477;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$The nurse plans care for a client after a femoral artery procedure and a client with a suspected DVT (deep vein thrombosis). Which items belong in the plan? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$The nurse plans care for a client after a femoral artery procedure and a client with a suspected DVT (deep vein thrombosis). Which items belong in the plan? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Notify the provider immediately if the six Ps develop"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Check pulses before and after interventions"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Observe the six Ps without escalating"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Massage the leg with the suspected DVT"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Do not massage the leg with the suspected DVT"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$The nurse does not massage a suspected DVT (deep vein thrombosis) leg, assesses pulses before and after interventions, and treats the six Ps as an arterial emergency that needs immediate provider notification.$nx$ WHERE id=3501;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with a T4 spinal cord injury has a heart rate of 48/min, a blood pressure of 82/50 mm Hg, and warm, dry skin. Which type of shock does the nurse suspect?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with a T4 spinal cord injury has a heart rate of 48/min, a blood pressure of 82/50 mm Hg, and warm, dry skin. Which type of shock does the nurse suspect?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Hypovolemic shock"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Cardiogenic shock"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Neurogenic shock"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Anaphylactic shock"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Neurogenic shock follows spinal injury with loss of sympathetic tone, causing low cardiac output, low systemic vascular resistance, bradycardia, hypotension, and warm, dry skin below the injury. Bradycardia with hypotension is the distinguishing pattern.$nx$ WHERE id=3609;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client after a motor vehicle crash is restless, with a heart rate of 118/min, a respiratory rate of 26/min, and a blood pressure of 112/70 mm Hg. Which interpretation by the nurse is MOST accurate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client after a motor vehicle crash is restless, with a heart rate of 118/min, a respiratory rate of 26/min, and a blood pressure of 112/70 mm Hg. Which interpretation by the nurse is MOST accurate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "A normal blood pressure rules out shock"}, {"id": "b", "text": "These findings are expected anxiety only"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The client may be in early shock, and trends matter more than one normal blood pressure"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Bradycardia is the first sign of shock"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Tachycardia comes first and the blood pressure falls late, so a normal blood pressure does not rule out shock. The nurse looks at trends rather than a single value.$nx$ WHERE id=3613;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with a gastrointestinal bleed is anxious and breathing fast, with a heart rate of 120/min and a normal blood pressure. Which action is MOST appropriate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with a gastrointestinal bleed is anxious and breathing fast, with a heart rate of 120/min and a normal blood pressure. Which action is MOST appropriate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Wait for hypotension to develop before acting"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Reassure the client because anxiety explains the findings"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Recognize compensated shock early and treat according to its cause"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Treat every type of shock the same way"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Early shock shows tachycardia, tachypnea and anxiety before hypotension. The nurse recognizes compensated shock early and tailors treatment to its mechanism.$nx$ WHERE id=3629;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nursing student asks why a normal blood pressure does not rule out shock. Which response by the nurse is correct?$nx$, question=$nx$A nursing student asks why a normal blood pressure does not rule out shock. Which response by the nurse is correct?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"A normal blood pressure after treatment confirms recovery.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Tachycardia comes first and the blood pressure drops late, so trends matter more than one value.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"A normal blood pressure definitely rules out shock.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"Bradycardia is the first sign of every type of shock.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$In shock, tachycardia appears first and blood pressure drops last, so a normal blood pressure does not exclude shock. Trends are more important than a single value.$nx$ WHERE id=3639;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client in septic shock is receiving a norepinephrine infusion. Which nursing action is MOST appropriate?$nx$, question=$nx$A client in septic shock is receiving a norepinephrine infusion. Which nursing action is MOST appropriate?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Stop caring about the shock type once oxygen is started"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Check the blood pressure once per shift"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Monitor peripheral perfusion while titrating to support systemic vascular resistance"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Expect bronchodilation because norepinephrine is a pure beta-2 drug"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Norepinephrine acts on alpha-1 and beta-1 receptors to raise systemic vascular resistance and is first-line for septic shock. The nurse monitors peripheral perfusion while titrating.$nx$ WHERE id=3651;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which statements about the early signs of shock are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$Which statements about the early signs of shock are accurate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Tachycardia is the first sign"}, {"id": "b", "text": "A drop in blood pressure is a late finding"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A normal blood pressure does not exclude early shock"}, {"id": "d", "text": "A normal blood pressure definitely excludes shock"}, {"id": "e", "text": "Bradycardia is the first sign of all shock"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Tachycardia comes first, and blood pressure drops last, so a normal blood pressure does not rule out shock.$nx$ WHERE id=3663;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse is caring for a client at risk for shock. Which statements are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse is caring for a client at risk for shock. Which statements are appropriate? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Compensated shock can appear before the blood pressure drops"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Delayed recognition raises the risk of multiple organ dysfunction syndrome"}, {"id": "c", "text": "All types of shock are treated the same way long term"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Hypotension must appear before any intervention"}, {"id": "e", "text": "After initial stabilization, treatment targets the type of shock"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Early shock shows tachycardia, tachypnea and anxiety before hypotension, and delayed recognition raises the risk of multiple organ dysfunction syndrome. After stabilization, definitive management is specific to the shock type.$nx$ WHERE id=3679;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client is being assessed for shock. Which principles apply? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$A client is being assessed for shock. Which principles apply? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "A drop in blood pressure is a late finding"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Bradycardia is the first sign of shock"}, {"id": "c", "text": "A normal blood pressure cannot exclude early shock"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Tachycardia appears first"}, {"id": "e", "text": "A normal blood pressure definitely excludes shock"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Tachycardia comes first and the blood pressure falls last, so a normal blood pressure cannot rule out early shock.$nx$ WHERE id=3689;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$Which critical values prompt an action by the nurse? Select all that apply.$nx$, question=$nx$Which critical values prompt an action by the nurse? Select all that apply.$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Temp above 38°C: obtain cultures before antibiotics"}, {"id": "b", "text": "HR (heart rate) below 60: hold digoxin or the beta-blocker"}, {"id": "c", "text": "RR (respiratory rate) below 12: give epinephrine"}, {"id": "d", "text": "BP (blood pressure) below 90/60: assess"}, {"id": "e", "text": "HR (heart rate) above 100: hold digoxin"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$BP (blood pressure) <90/60 = hypotension → assess; HR (heart rate) <60 = hold digoxin/BB; temp >38°C = fever → cultures before antibiotics.$nx$ WHERE id=4107;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A client with suspected COVID-19 (coronavirus disease 2019) is being admitted from the emergency department. Which room placement and precautions should the nurse arrange?$nx$, question=$nx$A client with suspected COVID-19 (coronavirus disease 2019) is being admitted from the emergency department. Which room placement and precautions should the nurse arrange?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "Airborne and contact precautions in a negative-pressure room"}, {"id": "b", "text": "Droplet precautions in a semi-private room"}, {"id": "c", "text": "Standard precautions in a positive-pressure room"}, {"id": "d", "text": "Contact precautions only in a standard room"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$SARS (severe acute respiratory syndrome) and COVID-19 (coronavirus disease 2019) require airborne plus contact precautions with an N95 respirator and a negative-pressure room. Droplet or contact precautions alone are insufficient.$nx$ WHERE id=17758;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nursing student states, "If I gave the care, it still counts even if I forget to document it." Which response by the instructor is best?$nx$, question=$nx$A nursing student states, "If I gave the care, it still counts even if I forget to document it." Which response by the instructor is best?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "\"Yes, as long as another nurse saw you give the care.\""}, {"id": "b", "text": "\"Yes, documenting care is optional when you are busy.\""}, {"id": "c", "text": "\"Yes, the client can confirm the care if anyone asks.\""}, {"id": "d", "text": "\"No, care that is not charted is considered not done.\""}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$The golden rule of charting is that if you didn't chart it, it didn't happen. Witnesses or client recall do not replace documentation.$nx$ WHERE id=19199;
UPDATE test_questions SET question_stem=$nx$A nurse is writing nursing diagnoses for a client's care plan. Which source should the nurse use for diagnosis labels?$nx$, question=$nx$A nurse is writing nursing diagnoses for a client's care plan. Which source should the nurse use for diagnosis labels?$nx$, options=$nx$[{"id": "a", "text": "The provider's list of medical diagnoses"}, {"id": "b", "text": "The client's laboratory report"}, {"id": "c", "text": "The client's own description of the disease"}, {"id": "d", "text": "The NANDA-I list of official terms"}]$nx$::jsonb, rationale=$nx$Nursing diagnoses should use the NANDA-I list, because only official terms are used for diagnoses. The provider's medical diagnoses are not nursing diagnoses.$nx$ WHERE id=19792;
